                <pb facs="0221" n="141" xml:id="pg141"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Translation from Peking Gazette, December 31,
                        1901.</hi></head>
                <p>On the 18th of the eleventh moon the following imperial edict was received:</p>
                <p>“According to a memorial of Prince Ch’ing and others, the ministers of Great
                    Britain and the United States have requested that Chang Yin-huan, who had
                    suffered punishment, might be rehabilitated, etc.</p>
                <p>“Let Chang Yin-huan, deceased, formerly the senior vice-president of the Board of
                    revenue, as a mark of special mercy, be restored to his former official status
                    in order to the promotion of friendly feelings.</p>
                <p>“Respect this.”</p>
            </div>
